-- Fork F50: the leave papers and the death papers, printed under 3 (traffic accidents), are
-- asked for whenever the claim is for a daily allowance or a death, whatever the accident.
GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A claim document`
`the documents Part VII asks for in` claim MEANS
    concat (LIST (LIST `a claim form stamped by the policyholder and signed by an authorised person`),
                 `for the treatment`,
                 `for an accident`,
                 `for a daily allowance`,
                 `for a death`)
    WHERE
        `when` b xs MEANS IF b THEN xs ELSE EMPTY
        `items` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
            WHEN `medical expenses` t is THEN is
            OTHERWISE EMPTY
        `some item` h MEANS any (GIVEN i YIELD i's `head` EQUALS h) `items`
        `for the treatment` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
            WHEN `medical expenses` t is THEN
                IF   t's `setting` EQUALS `outpatient treatment`
                THEN concat (LIST (LIST `the medical record book or examination slip`, `invoices for examination and tests, itemised`),
                                  `when` (`some item` `medicine`) (LIST `the prescription`, `invoices for medicine`),
                                  `when` (`some item` `tests, ultrasound, X-ray and CT scans`) (LIST `the indications and results of tests`))
                ELSE concat (LIST (LIST `the discharge paper`, `invoices for the hospital stay`),
                                  `when` (`some item` `surgery`) (LIST `the surgery certificate`),
                                  `when` (claim's `the file`'s `an invoice lumps several kinds of cost together`) (LIST `an itemised statement of hospital fees`),
                                  `when` (`some item` `tests in the 30 days before admission`)
                                         (LIST `the indications and results of tests before admission`, `invoices for tests before admission, with an itemised statement`),
                                  `when` (`some item` `treatment in the 45 days after discharge`)
                                         (LIST `the indication for follow-up after discharge`, `invoices for follow-up after discharge`))
            OTHERWISE EMPTY
        `for an accident` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the file`'s `kind of accident`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
            WHEN JUST k THEN
                CONSIDER k
                WHEN `an accident at work`       THEN LIST `an accident report confirmed and stamped by the policyholder`
                WHEN `an accident in daily life` THEN LIST `an accident report by the insured or the beneficiary`
                WHEN `a traffic accident`        THEN
                    append (`when` (claim's `the file`'s `a serious traffic accident, fatal or involving a third party`)
                                   (LIST `an accident record confirmed by the police or the local authority`))
                           (LIST `copies of the driving licence and vehicle registration`)
        `for a daily allowance` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
            WHEN `daily allowance` d THEN LIST `the doctor's indication of leave, and HR's confirmation of the days off`
            OTHERWISE EMPTY
        `for a death` MEANS
            CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
            WHEN `death` h THEN LIST `the death certificate, and papers proving the right to inherit`
            OTHERWISE EMPTY

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A claim document`
`the documents missing from` claim MEANS
    filter (GIVEN d YIELD NOT elem d (claim's `the file`'s `documents supplied`)) (`the documents Part VII asks for in` claim)

-- Note: a VAT (financial) invoice is needed for a medical cost of VND 200.000 or more.
-- 200.000 is two hundred thousand (the dot groups thousands).
-- src:1144 | Chú ý: Cần có hóa đơn VAT (hóa đơn tài chính) cho chi phí y tế từ 200.000 VNĐ trở lên.
GIVEN item IS AN `An item of expense`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `lacks the VAT invoice it needs` item IF
        item's `amount` AT LEAST 200000
    AND NOT item's `with a VAT invoice`

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `An item of expense`
`the items lacking a VAT invoice in` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `the outcome`
    WHEN `medical expenses` t items THEN filter `lacks the VAT invoice it needs` items
    OTHERWISE EMPTY

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim file is complete in` claim IF
        null (`the documents missing from` claim)
    AND null (`the items lacking a VAT invoice in` claim)

§§ `The signature and the claim form`

-- The rules are signed for the corporation by a deputy general director (lines 1145-1151).
-- The claim form (lines 1155-1225) is a blank form: the facts it asks for are the inputs of
-- this encoding (the insured, the event, the treatment, the documents, the payment details);
-- it states no rule. Inert.
